#edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71bb7beb-a9ec-524e-b310-db15c4e11f3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-338023" :question/problem "Select all homogeneous second-order linear differential equations.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ which is different from zero.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy-{e}^{x}=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)={e}^{x},$ which is different from zero."}] [17592186311914 {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152274}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2552a4d9-f78f-5d7c-ba54-94ce2e3d49c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755803} {:answer/id #uuid "938ee41a-af05-5b09-873f-ba86a46017f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "938ee41a-af05-5b09-873f-ba86a46017f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755804} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9251bf7-8183-5579-89dd-1bad45029dc2" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+(x-2){y}^{′}+y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755802} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf5c5d6f-5ccb-5d4f-bc88-5ab55e86ea42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755806} {:answer/id #uuid "a15763ad-367c-54f7-b3f3-1fbdbb663026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a15763ad-367c-54f7-b3f3-1fbdbb663026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755807} :answer-field/id #uuid "076df855-d1d0-58a5-bdca-0e10426c7bcc" :answer-field/key "$({x}^{2}+1){y}^{″}-4x{y}^{′}+3y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fffa315-2e94-5fd9-acd6-b6857ffe0b34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755809} {:answer/id #uuid "a6fca151-c97b-5c7f-9fb5-403f136864a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fffa315-2e94-5fd9-acd6-b6857ffe0b34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755809} :answer-field/id #uuid "60587c19-80f2-51d9-9c31-b07785fb9c65" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,y+9=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5eca540-4772-55d6-813f-fd6cd2026d5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-338087" :question/problem "Select all homogeneous second-order linear differential equations.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+(x-2){y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+1){y}^{″}-4x{y}^{′}+3y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,y+9=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,y=-9.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-9,$ which is different from zero."}] [17592186397097 {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397097 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152274}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f14af8af-5806-5342-acc3-45f3c5f3dad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755767} {:answer/id #uuid "2f5bf1eb-28eb-5a44-9dd0-7b13e50f5ab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f5bf1eb-28eb-5a44-9dd0-7b13e50f5ab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755768} :answer-field/id #uuid "edebfcf6-8a44-52a9-9d58-0b395090d784" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6240e0e5-6564-540e-9c4b-dfce1245c6ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755770} {:answer/id #uuid "751b6ce6-dafa-5a22-bb84-85bb0be36cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6240e0e5-6564-540e-9c4b-dfce1245c6ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755770} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cc8e66e-b5e7-57da-ae09-cdf15853acb5" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}=x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f90e140a-c1af-5297-9393-f5f1546f071f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755773} {:answer/id #uuid "328fdd7b-9b76-5795-9b0d-0754f5d46d42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f90e140a-c1af-5297-9393-f5f1546f071f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755773} :answer-field/id #uuid "aabaaeee-0cdb-509c-a1c9-b909c583f28c" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}-xy+4x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8da06f22-6a38-578e-b590-3e2d4a9025f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-338004" :question/problem "Select all homogeneous second-order linear differential equations.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-xy+4x=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-xy=-4x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-4x,$ which is different from zero."}] [17592186397107 {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397107 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152274}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b08425c2-a62a-59a0-8d61-2be0c43d1bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755794} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e83836-5039-5c26-b254-f0b9ac803ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b08425c2-a62a-59a0-8d61-2be0c43d1bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755794} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4c87c84-9c19-5e01-98e7-3216d34337f0" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+2y=x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755793} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c2b6982-ae03-5ccd-8333-82ce10c73f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755797} {:answer/id #uuid "fb1cd29a-2c74-5d0f-9b03-e55e99764d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb1cd29a-2c74-5d0f-9b03-e55e99764d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755798} :answer-field/id #uuid "5253b071-4f14-5118-8a5d-78122d58e646" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x){y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-6y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755796} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85ee9fbd-d4d8-551b-b592-e505d97cd355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755800} {:answer/id #uuid "ea1fbee0-fdc7-5ee3-ad2d-02b56e6d421b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85ee9fbd-d4d8-551b-b592-e505d97cd355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755800} :answer-field/id #uuid "763ea887-1956-5711-977e-a06d65fc4e89" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}-(x+2)y+5x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8b12875-ae8a-5464-b1d4-8be3ec87c5f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-338082" :question/problem "Select all homogeneous second-order linear differential equations.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2y=x\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x){y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-6y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-(x+2)y+5x=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-(x+2)y=-5x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-5x,$ which is different from zero."}]]
